## Layout Patterns

### 1. Centered Content with Max Width
```dart
Padding(
  padding: L.pageGutter,
  child: Center(
    child: ConstrainedBox(
      constraints: BoxConstraints(
        maxWidth: L.isDesktop ? 1000 : (L.isTablet ? 720 : double.infinity),
      ),
      child: child,
    ),
  ),
)
```

### 2. Responsive Grid
```dart
GridView.builder(
  gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
    crossAxisCount: L.columnsFor(280),  // Auto-calculate columns
    crossAxisSpacing: L.spaceM,
    mainAxisSpacing: L.spaceM,
  ),
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => GridItem(),
)
```

### 3. Responsive AppBar
```dart
SliverAppBar(
  toolbarHeight: L.isDesktop ? L.rem(9) : L.rem(7),
  expandedHeight: (0.22.h(context)).clamp(180.0, 260.0),
  leading: Icon(Icons.arrow_back, size: L.iconM),
  title: Text('Dashboard'),
)
```

### 4. Responsive Container
```dart
Container(
  width: L.responsiveSize(
    phone: 100,
    tablet: 150,
    desktop: 200,
  ),
  height: L.responsiveSize(
    phone: 50,
    tablet: 60,
    desktop: 70,
  ),
  child: child,
)
```

## Animation System

### Responsive Durations
```dart
AnimatedContainer(
  duration: L.fast,               // 90-140ms (scale-aware)
  child: child,
)

AnimatedOpacity(
  duration: L.normal,             // 160-240ms (scale-aware)
  opacity: opacity,
  child: child,
)

AnimatedPositioned(
  duration: L.slow,               // 260-380ms (scale-aware)
  child: child,
)
```

## Touch Targets

### Minimum Touch Target
```dart
Container(
  width: L.minTapTarget,          // 44px (phone) / 48px (tablet+)
  height: L.minTapTarget,
  child: child,
)
```

### Hit Slop
```dart
GestureDetector(
  onTap: () {},
  child: Container(
    padding: L.hitSlop,           // 4px all around
    child: child,
  ),
)
```

## Breakpoint Helpers

### Quick Flags
```dart
if (L.isCompact) {
  // Small phone layout
} else if (L.isMobile) {
  // Phone layout
} else if (L.isTablet) {
  // Tablet layout
} else if (L.isDesktop) {
  // Desktop layout
}
```

### Device-Specific Code
```dart
switch (context.device) {
  case DeviceSize.phone:
    return PhoneLayout();
  case DeviceSize.tablet:
    return TabletLayout();
  case DeviceSize.desktop:
    return DesktopLayout();
}
```

## Common Patterns

### 1. Responsive Card Grid
```dart
GridView.builder(
  gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
    crossAxisCount: L.isDesktop ? 4 : (L.isTablet ? 3 : 2),
    crossAxisSpacing: L.spaceM,
    mainAxisSpacing: L.spaceM,
  ),
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => Card(),
)
```

### 2. Responsive List
```dart
ListView.builder(
  padding: L.pageGutter,
  itemExtent: L.isDesktop ? 80 : 60,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => ListTile(),
)
```

### 3. Responsive Bottom Sheet
```dart
showModalBottomSheet(
  context: context,
  isScrollControlled: true,
  builder: (context) => Container(
    height: L.isDesktop ? 400 : MediaQuery.of(context).size.height * 0.7,
    child: BottomSheetContent(),
  ),
)
```

## Performance Considerations

### 1. Single MediaQuery Read
The responsive system reads MediaQuery only once at the top level, making deep widget trees efficient.

### 2. Inherited Widget Pattern
Uses InheritedWidget for efficient updates - only widgets that depend on changed values rebuild.

### 3. Const Constructors
Always use const constructors where possible to prevent unnecessary rebuilds.

### 4. Responsive Caching
The system caches computed values and only recalculates when screen size changes.

## Testing Responsive Design

### 1. Test Different Breakpoints
```dart
testWidgets('should adapt to tablet layout', (tester) async {
  await tester.binding.setSurfaceSize(Size(800, 600));
  await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
  // Test tablet-specific behavior
});
```

### 2. Test Orientation Changes
```dart
testWidgets('should handle orientation change', (tester) async {
  await tester.binding.setSurfaceSize(Size(400, 800)); // Portrait
  await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
  
  await tester.binding.setSurfaceSize(Size(800, 400)); // Landscape
  await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
});
```